  "question": "Stock Trading System\n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe Stock Trading System is an automated platform designed to manage the trading of stocks for publicly traded companies. The system simplifies search, purchase, and management of stock holdings through individual user portfolios.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- Facilitate efficient trading of stocks.\n- Streamline the management of user portfolios.\n- Ensure secure and accurate processing of transactions across multiple exchanges.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Traders: Individuals who own and trade stocks through brokerages.\n- Brokers: Entities that facilitate stock trades between traders and exchanges.\n- Stock Exchanges: Platforms where stocks are listed and traded.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Company Management: \n  - Manage company information, including name, headquarters address, and established date.\n  - Each public company is associated with a unique stock.\n\n- Stock Trading:\n  - Each stock is identified by a unique stock code and possible to be traded on up to 9 exchanges.\n  - Stocks are associated with symbols unique to each exchange.\n  - Record last trading price and daily volume per symbol.\n\n- Trader and Account Management:\n  - Traders have unique IDs and may own multiple accounts.\n  - Accounts hold securities and cash, and are linked to specific brokers.\n\n- Broker Management:\n  - Brokers manage trades and pay exchange fees.\n  - Manage broker information, including contact details and state.\n\n- Transaction Management:\n  - Allow traders to place orders and process through brokerages.\n  - Each transaction records number of shares, price, commissions, and a timestamp.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: Efficient handling of high-volume transactions.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of user data and trading executions.\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of traders and stock exchanges.\n- Reliability: Accurate record-keeping and transaction processing are crucial.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0160\nCREATE TABLE `company` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `headquarters_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `established_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stock` (\n  `stock_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stock_code`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_stock_company` (`company_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stock_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `company` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stock_exchange` (\n  `exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exchange_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_stock_exchange_code` (`exchange_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stock_listing` (\n  `listing_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `symbol` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `last_trading_price` decimal(18,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `daily_volume` bigint(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`listing_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_stock_listing_exchange_symbol` (`exchange_id`,`symbol`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_stock_listing_stock_exchange` (`stock_code`,`exchange_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stock_listing_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`stock_code`) REFERENCES `stock` (`stock_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stock_listing_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`exchange_id`) REFERENCES `stock_exchange` (`exchange_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `broker` (\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`broker_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trader` (\n  `trader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trader_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`trader_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trading_account` (\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cash_balance` decimal(18,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0.00',\n  `security_value` decimal(18,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0.00',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`account_id`),\n  KEY `trading_account_ibfk_1` (`trader_id`),\n  KEY `trading_account_ibfk_2` (`broker_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trading_account_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`trader_id`) REFERENCES `trader` (`trader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trading_account_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`broker_id`) REFERENCES `broker` (`broker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trade_transaction` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `listing_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `shares` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(18,4) NOT NULL,\n  `commission` decimal(18,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0.00',\n  `transaction_timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  KEY `trade_transaction_ibfk_1` (`account_id`),\n  KEY `trade_transaction_ibfk_2` (`listing_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trade_transaction_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `trading_account` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trade_transaction_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`listing_id`) REFERENCES `stock_listing` (`listing_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
